																		The Gods of the SCP Universe
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/baronjoe" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3376201); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3376201&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606724593" alt="Baronjoe" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3376201)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/baronjoe" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3376201); return false;" >Baronjoe</a></span> <span class="odate time_1519189722 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Feb 2018 05:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3717205">
									

<p>So let's discuss some gods that exist in the SCP Universe. Lets start with&#8230;</p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Eldritch Horrors/Lovecraftian</span>:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The Scarlet King:</strong> Pretty much a more Lovecraftian version of the devil and is heavily involved in SCP-231.</li>
<li><strong>Yaldabaoth:</strong> A flesh god/goddess that Sarkic Cults worship that has six loyal Archons.</li>
<li><strong>The Hanged King of Alagadda:</strong> A being which rules the land of Alagadda which is also known as SCP-2264 and connected to SCP-701, the Hanged King's Tragedy.</li>
<li><strong>The Star Fish:</strong> I don't know particularly much about this one but it's a part of the Fifthist Church which is an odd group.</li>
<li><strong>The Cicada God:</strong> A divine cicada also known as SCP-3004 and it believes to be the Abrahamic god.</li>
<li><strong>SCP-3999:</strong> Pretty much madness incarnate.</li>
<li><strong>SCP-582:</strong> An eldritch horror that has no will and has many forms. It's actions is up to the writer who writes about it.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Other SCPverse Deities</span>:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>He-Who-Made-Light and He-Who-Made-Dark:</strong> &quot;Long ago, when the world was only water and sky, there were two brothers, “He-Who-Made-Light” and “He-Who-Made-Dark.” Like all brothers they fought. One time the light brother insulted the work of the dark brother. The dark one, he does not like this, and begins to destroy all the light in the world&#8230;&quot;</li>
<li><strong>Pangloss:</strong> Benevolent and leaves quite enjoyable notes. He is also named The Flame</li>
<li><strong>Mekhane:</strong> The Church of the Broken God's deity that is a god of machines.</li>
<li><strong>Saint Alagadda:</strong> Not really known but is likely where the city Alagadda got its name from.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Hinduism</span>:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Kali:</strong> Kali is the goddess of destruction and doesn't appear directly. She appears through her avatar known as SCP-029.</li>
<li><strong>Anantashesha:</strong> It is up to interpretation if SCP-3000 is really Anantashesha. Personally, I kinda doubt that and have a small head canon that 3000 just influenced the idea of Shesha.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Abrahamic/Hebrew</span>:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The Creator/God/343:</strong> Well, SCP-343 claims to be the one god but that is debatable. Personally, I think of him as somewhat of an avatar.</li>
<li><strong>Moloch:</strong> Sacrifices are to be made to a statue of Moloch that is SCP-089. Failure results in catastrophe.</li>
</ul>
<p>So yeah, anything else?</p>

