														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3719326">
									

<p>So the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/second-hytoth#pages">Church of the Second Hytoth</a>/Ortothan mythos I've been working has been building up a ton of gods. Only one of them appears as a skip though. For the sake of time this list won't have every detail I've envisioned (more details are in some of the articles), so here are the more prominent gods:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Lore&nbsp;galore</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Lore&nbsp;galore</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Main Ortothan Mythos Gods</strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The Koru-teusa:</strong> The Holy Seven. Seven alien mortals from a now destroyed universe (the 'First Hytoth'), who ascended to godhood and decided to protect the universe from extrauniversal threats (and anything that could threaten themselves or their followers).
<ul>
<li><strong>Zeyu-leusan:</strong> The Holy First. Sacrificed themselves to stop a massive extrauniversal incursion.</li>
<li><strong>Urkot-leusan:</strong> The Holy Second. Killed in a feud with Eov-Leusan.</li>
<li><strong>Eov-leusan:</strong> The Holy Third. Killed in a feud with Urkot-leusan.</li>
<li><strong>Rakmou-leusan:</strong> The Holy Fourth. Currently guarding a hole in the universe and fighting extrauniversal threats. The only surviving member of the Koru-teusa.</li>
<li><strong>Holy Fifth:</strong> Currently unnamed. Status unknown.</li>
<li><strong>Yorun-leusan:</strong> The Holy Sixth. Former protector of the Eitoth (an afterlife of sorts). Killed during an extrauniversal incursion.</li>
<li><strong>Holy Seventh:</strong> Currently unnamed. Status unknown; presumed by many to have been wiped out of existence.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>The Nameless Creator:</strong> An extrauniversal &quot;thing&quot; that made the First Hytoth and the Second Hytoth (the current universe). Its intent in creating the universes, whether it is still alive, and whether it is still active is unknown.</li>
<li><strong>The One of Dark and the One of Light:</strong> Two primordial gods from the First Hytoth, one representing darkness and the other light.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-152348-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-152348-1')">1</a></sup></li>
<li><strong>The Voruteut:</strong> Not exactly gods but a collection of extrauniversal creatures, deities, and assorted monstrosities that lurk in the space outside the universe (the Voru). This is what the Koru-teusa had been fighting.</li>
<li><strong>???:</strong> An unknown extrauniversal &quot;thing&quot; that ate the First Hytoth, destroying it. Status unknown.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Other Gods/Deities</strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wonlaik the Trickster:</strong> A trickster deity that was killed by Rakmou-leusan after their japes went too far.</li>
<li><strong>Kornoct:</strong> A deity that watches over the Eitoth, essentially serving as its internal security.</li>
<li><strong>Uravol the Bodiless:</strong> A minor psionic deity in the First Hytoth that went on a massive power trip, killing two of the strongest First Hytoth gods before becoming mentally broken and cast out of any physical form. Status unknown.</li>
<li><strong>Nohlos:</strong> An ancient First Hytoth god that existed before the universe, eating the reality around itself as it moved through space. Broken into <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2742">SCP-2742</a> instances after Uravol attempted to kill it.</li>
<li><strong>The God King of the Stars:</strong> A powerful god/dictator in the Second Hytoth.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-152348-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-152348-2')">2</a></sup></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-152348-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-152348-1')">1</a>. Loosely based on He-Who-Made-Dark and He-He-Made-Light. It doesn't entirely line up with the authorcanon behind those so I now view them as different things.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-152348-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-152348-2')">2</a>. Currently based on <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2998">Adidal</a>.</div>
</div>

