			<div class="content" id="post-content-3916856">
									

<p>The recent <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/bird">Team Bird</a> series features a few different deities and acknowledges them as gods. They are as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Thoth:</strong> The central deity and antagonist <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-sacred-djehuti">Thoth AKA Sacred Djehuti</a> is a manipulative trickster god, the very same one worshipped by the Egyptians. He imposed his will on the entire human race and conquers worlds to find vassals worthy of his paradise.</li>
<li><strong>Medila:</strong> As featured in <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/SCP-3095">SCP-3095</a>. Medila is an Avian deity that bestows wisdom and intelligence to birds worldwide. Some of the birds affected by this become intelligent enough to be recognized as members of the Foundation, forming the Avian Division.</li>
<li><strong>Akheilos:</strong> As featured in <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/spc-507">SPC-507</a>. Known to the Shark Punching Centre as WHITE NETHER, Akheilos is a chaotic Selachian deity that consumes knowledge and is an eternal enemy of Thoth.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>The Mistaken Beast:</strong> (Not actually featured in this series, just alluded to.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-751497-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-751497-1')">1</a></sup>) The creator of Akheilos. The Mistaken Beast is a universal Selachian monster that threatens to heavily distort each and every universe, one by one, upon awakening. Sharks are an inherent implausability and humorous plague on reality; the SPC punches them to keep the Mistaken Beast asleep.</li>
</ul>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-751497-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-751497-1')">1</a>. The Mistaken Beast can be found referenced in the various <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/shark-punching-center#pages">Shark Punching Center</a> GoI formats on the Wiki.</div>
</div>

